# i18n sync (Novel Work)

UI strings live in `src/i18n/messages.ts`. Supported locales: `en`, `zh-CN`, `zh-TW`, `ja`, `de`, `fr`. Preference `system` follows OS language.

When you add or change user-visible text:

1. Add/update the key in `zhCN` (source of truth).
2. Update the **same key** in `en`, `zhTW`, `ja`, `de`, and `fr` in the same change.
3. Use `useI18n().t('key')` or `t('key', { param })` in Vue—do not hardcode new UI strings.
4. Do not leave a new key only in one language.

Backend/LLM prompts may stay Chinese unless the task asks otherwise; this rule is for the app UI.
